	<!-- ─── Calibration & Interference Guide ───────────────── -->
	<section id="calibration" class="border-t border-hairline bg-canvas scroll-mt-16">
		<div class="mx-auto max-w-[1200px] px-4 py-20 sm:px-6 md:py-28">
			<div class="grid gap-12 lg:grid-cols-2 lg:items-center">
				<div>
					<p class="eyebrow">precision troubleshooting</p>
					<h2 class="mt-3 text-display-lg text-ink">Mastering Magnetometer Calibration & Interference</h2>
					<p class="mt-4 text-body-lg text-body leading-relaxed">
						Unlike an optical camera or a GPS satellite receiver, an electronic magnetometer does not measure an isolated signal—it measures the composite summation of <em>every magnetic vector in the room</em>.
					</p>
					<p class="mt-4 text-sm text-body leading-6">
						To understand why calibration matters, electrical engineers divide magnetic distortion into two categories:
					</p>

					<div class="mt-6 space-y-4">
						<div class="rounded-xl border border-hairline bg-canvas-soft/50 p-4">
							<h3 class="text-sm font-semibold text-ink">Hard Iron Distortion</h3>
							<p class="mt-1 text-xs text-body leading-5">
								Generated by permanent magnetized materials attached to the phone itself (internal speaker coils, camera optical stabilization magnets, and MagSafe case rings). This creates a static, permanent directional offset that shifts the center point of the magnetic coordinate sphere.
							</p>
						</div>
						<div class="rounded-xl border border-hairline bg-canvas-soft/50 p-4">
							<h3 class="text-sm font-semibold text-ink">Soft Iron Distortion</h3>
							<p class="mt-1 text-xs text-body leading-5">
								Generated by passive ferromagnetic materials (structural steel I-beams, rebar in concrete floors, car doors, and cast iron radiators) that warp Earth's uniform field into an irregular ellipse.
							</p>
						</div>
					</div>

					<p class="mt-6 text-sm text-body leading-6">
						The famous <strong>"Figure-8 Motion"</strong> is not a superstitious ritual—it is a mathematical algorithm. Moving your phone through a 3D figure-eight forces the sensor through every quadrant of space, allowing the operating system's Kalman matrix to plot an ellipsoidal locus and calculate the precise offset transformation required to snap the data back into a true spherical coordinate frame.
					</p>
				</div>

				<div class="card-soft p-6 sm:p-8">
					<h3 class="text-display-sm text-ink mb-6">4-Step Precision Calibration Checklist</h3>
					<ol class="space-y-6">
						<li class="flex gap-4">
							<span class="flex h-7 w-7 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-ink text-xs font-mono font-bold text-on-primary">1</span>
							<div>
								<h4 class="text-sm font-semibold text-ink">Isolate Metallic Accessories</h4>
								<p class="mt-1 text-xs text-body leading-5">Remove magnetic wallet sleeves, cases with metal kickstands, and stay at least 1.5 meters away from desktop computers, running automobile engines, and audio speakers.</p>
							</div>
						</li>
						<li class="flex gap-4">
							<span class="flex h-7 w-7 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-ink text-xs font-mono font-bold text-on-primary">2</span>
							<div>
								<h4 class="text-sm font-semibold text-ink">Rest in Horizontal Palm</h4>
								<p class="mt-1 text-xs text-body leading-5">Hold the phone screen facing upward in the flat palm of your hand, keeping the chassis parallel to the ground to maximize the horizontal field vector.</p>
							</div>
						</li>
						<li class="flex gap-4">
							<span class="flex h-7 w-7 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-ink text-xs font-mono font-bold text-on-primary">3</span>
							<div>
								<h4 class="text-sm font-semibold text-ink">Execute the 3D Figure-Eight</h4>
								<p class="mt-1 text-xs text-body leading-5">Rotate your wrist through a smooth infinity symbol (∞) motion, pitching and rolling the phone for 8–10 seconds until the accuracy indicator turns green.</p>
							</div>
						</li>
						<li class="flex gap-4">
							<span class="flex h-7 w-7 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-ink text-xs font-mono font-bold text-on-primary">4</span>
							<div>
								<h4 class="text-sm font-semibold text-ink">Cross-Check with the Solar Azimuth</h4>
